        "narration": "An ancient crater lake changed color in just two to three days. India's Lake Lonar swapped its characteristic green water for a striking shade of pink.",
        "visual_query": "lonar crater lake india aerial",
        "visual_fallback": "pink lake aerial view"
      },
      {
        "narration": "This wasn't chemical runoff. Satellites confirmed the massive, four-hundred-foot-deep basin changed color across just two days.",
        "visual_query": "deep impact crater lake landscape",
        "visual_fallback": "aerial view crater lake"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Did something ancient wake up in the sediment? Reports showed that falling water levels caused a sharp increase in salinity.",
        "visual_query": "water sample scientific test flask",
        "visual_fallback": "dark lake water surface"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Lab results revealed the culprit: extreme drought. Intense heat rapidly evaporated water, causing billions of salt-loving haloarchaea microbes to multiply.",
        "visual_query": "microscope lab petri dish science",
        "visual_fallback": "science laboratory microscope"
      },
      {
        "narration": "These tiny organisms produce pink carotenoid pigments to absorb sunlight, turning the ancient crater into a glowing neon phenomenon.",
